{"game": "roboquest", "language": "english", "appid": 692890, "month": "2020-11", "window": 2, "start_date": 1604793600, "end_date": 1605484799, "month_true_total": 78, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-03 01:48:04 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "79319717", "author": {"steamid": "76561198016127010", "personaname": "Mischail", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/mischail/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 80, "playtime_forever": 7786, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 302, "last_played": 1733183040, "avatar": "7b74ec4e6012c5b782ae0f41d9e0b7fc175177f6"}, "language": "english", "review": "Was a fun game until they've added final and final-final bosses with tons of preparation for it. The boss itself is pretty much everything I love: constant and infinite spam of everything you can imagine, making you feel like you play some dance simulator instead of fps shooter + hack and stun. Pretty easy if you have shield or teleport, but 4/6 classes are basically useless against it. There is nothing like playing the game for 40 minutes, reaching the final-final boss with 100% hp, and then instantly losing half of it to a single spam attack. And that's just on standard difficulty.\n\nIt's actually that bad, that you basically have to scrap every single fun ability you want to pick during the game and focus solely on the build for the final boss. Was way more fun in EA.", "timestamp_created": 1605463529, "timestamp_updated": 1699831472, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1597939791", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "79277443", "author": {"steamid": "76561197981493384", "personaname": "Cannon Fodder", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com